{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed402918419/2/codegen_prompts/4.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed402918419/2`\n- 题号：`4`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed402918419/2/4.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"4\">\n- `description`：识别每个对象的对称类型，按对称类型分组后，将同组对象堆叠合并为一个复合形状。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为黑色（black）。\n  - 网格中散布若干个由不同颜色构成的小型 4 连通对象，对象之间互不接触。\n  - 每个对象属于以下三种对称类型之一：仅有水平对称轴、仅有垂直对称轴、同时具有水平和垂直对称轴（含正方形等高度对称形状）。\n  - 同一对称类型的对象数量相同（例如每种类型各 2 个）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 第一步（分类）：将所有对象按其对称类型分为三组。\n  - 第二步（排列合并）：将每组内的对象按其在输入中从上到下、从左到右的出现顺序，在输出中紧密水平排列（对象之间无间隔），形成一个合并行。\n  - 第三步（输出布局）：三组合并行按\"双轴对称组在顶行、水平对称组在中行、垂直对称组在底行\"的固定顺序从上到下排列，行间留一行黑色背景。输出宽度为最宽合并行的宽度，不足的行右侧用黑色填充。\n\n- `Key insight`：表面上对象的颜色和位置各不相同，但真正的分组依据是形状的对称性质——解题者必须识别每个对象的对称类型才能确定分组，再根据分组规则完成排列。对称性分类是一个需要主动推理的非显然步骤。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/8abad3cf, train/6350f1f4, eval/62593bfd, train/5d588b4d, eval/332f06d7, eval/0934a4d8, eval/3e6067c3, eval/dbff022c\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8abad3cf\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3314\nmechanism=0.4834\nlexical=0.0135\ncode_feature=0.0000\noverlap_tags=object:sprite, object:square, operation:count, operation:sort_order, relation:adjacent, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/8abad3cf.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/8abad3cf.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRepack each non-background color group as a solid square ordered by increasing size.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid has one dominant background color, and each other color has a\nperfect-square pixel count. Those square side lengths are unique.\n\nRule\nConvert every non-background color into a filled square whose side length is\nthe square root of its pixel count. Place the squares from left to right in\nincreasing side length, bottom-aligned, with one background column between\nneighboring squares.\n\nKey insight\nThe original geometry of each color is discarded; only the color's total\npixel count determines the size of its packed output square.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"non-background color groups with perfect-square pixel counts\",\n  \"dst\": \"bottom-aligned solid color squares packed left-to-right\",\n  \"transform\": \"replace each color group by a filled square of the same color and area, with one background column between neighboring squares\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"order the squares by increasing side length; side lengths are unique\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"height is the largest square side; width is the sum of square sides plus one gap between each pair\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6350f1f4\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2978\nmechanism=0.3324\nlexical=0.0160\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:rotation, object:sprite, object:square, operation:reflect, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/6350f1f4.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/6350f1f4.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDecode a block-grid image by swapping each sprite-coded cell with a solid cell and each blank cell with the sprite.\n\nInput structure\nThe grid is partitioned by black separator rows and columns into equal-size\nsquare blocks. Each block is either a copy of one two-color sprite or a\nuniform blank block of the sprite's minority color; grey pixels are erased\ncells that act as wildcards.\n\nRule\nInfer the repeated sprite from fully visible mixed-color blocks. Replace a\nblock matching that sprite, ignoring grey erasures, with a solid block of\nthe sprite's majority color. Replace a uniform blank block with the sprite.\nSeparator rows and columns, including grey erasures on them, become black.\n\nKey insight\nThe small sprite is a block-level code for one macro-cell state, and the\nuniform minority-color block is the other state; the output renders the\nopposite code in each macro-cell while cleaning erased pixels.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"regular block grid separated by black lines; each block is either a two-color sprite or a uniform blank block, with grey pixels as erasures\",\n  \"dst\": \"same block grid with the two block states swapped\",\n  \"transform\": \"infer the sprite from fully visible mixed-color blocks; sprite-coded blocks become solid majority-color blocks, blank blocks become the sprite, and separator/erasure pixels become black\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"62593bfd\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3257\nmechanism=0.3742\nlexical=0.0133\ncode_feature=0.5714\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:rotation, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:reflect, operation:sort_order, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/62593bfd.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/62593bfd.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSort objects to top or bottom edge by whether their shape (up to rotation/flip) is shared.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Several multicolor connected components (8-connected) scattered across the grid.\n\nRule:\n- Compute each object's canonical shape (binary mask, invariant to rotation and flip).\n- Objects whose shape appears in two or more components → translate to TOP edge (row 0).\n- Objects whose shape is unique → translate to BOTTOM edge (row H−h).\n- Horizontal position (left column) is preserved; only vertical translation changes.\n\nKey insight: The sorting criterion is shape frequency (rotation-invariant), not area — duplicated shapes go up, unique shapes go down.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_in_order\",\n  \"src\": \"all connected components (objects) on the background\",\n  \"dst\": \"translate each object d vertically to an edge (x preserved)\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"group objects by their pixel-count (area). If an area value occurs >=2 times, those objects go to the TOP edge; if the area is unique, that object goes to the BOTTOM edge\",\n  \"transform\": \"duplicated-size -> top; singleton-size -> bottom\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5d588b4d\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3191\nmechanism=0.4653\nlexical=0.0138\ncode_feature=0.0000\noverlap_tags=object:sprite, operation:count, operation:reflect, operation:sort_order, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/5d588b4d.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/5d588b4d.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nExpand the top-left horizontal bar into a wrapped sequence of increasing and decreasing foreground runs.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a background color and exactly one foreground color.\n- All foreground pixels form one contiguous horizontal bar in the top row.\n- The bar starts at the left edge; its length is the control value n.\n\nRule:\n- Build a one-dimensional sequence of foreground runs with lengths\n  1, 2, ..., n, n-1, ..., 2, 1.\n- Separate adjacent runs by one background pixel.\n- Wrap the sequence row-major across the input width and pad the final row\n  with background pixels.\n\nKey insight:\nThe output preserves the input width; the bar length controls the run-length\ndiamond, and the apparent 2D pattern is just that 1D sequence wrapped into rows.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"symmetry/pattern\",\n  \"src\": \"the top-left horizontal foreground bar; its length n controls the run pattern\",\n  \"transform\": \"replace the grid with foreground runs of lengths 1, 2, ..., n, n-1, ..., 2, 1 separated by one background pixel and wrapped row-major across the input width\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"input width, minimum height needed for the wrapped sequence\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"332f06d7\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2834\nmechanism=0.3238\nlexical=0.0161\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, object:square, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/332f06d7.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/332f06d7.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide a solid square through a winding channel to reach a same-sized target square.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg (most common color). A river color forms a winding corridor.\n- Two same-sized NxN solid squares on the river: mover and destination, each a distinct color.\n\nRule:\n- The mover square travels along the river toward the destination.\n- It can only pass through positions where the full NxN area is river.\n- If reachable, the mover replaces the destination; otherwise it stops at the farthest reachable point.\n- The mover's original position is filled with the river color.\n\nKey insight: Chokepoints narrower than N pixels block the square, forcing it to stop short.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"black square\",\n  \"path\": \"blue pixels \\\"water channel\\\" that is wide enough to pass through until \\\"stuck\\\" because of too narrow\",\n  \"dst\": \"reach same sized red square or \\\"get stuck\\\" on the way where the blue path is too narrow\",\n  \"transform\": \"cover the red square if reaching it\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"0934a4d8\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2913\nmechanism=0.3659\nlexical=0.0126\ncode_feature=0.3333\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, object:sprite, object:square, operation:count, operation:reflect, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
